module gunbc.ci.ci_run_step_target

import std.types { String }
import std.optional { Optional, Present, Absent }
import std.coercion { unicode_scalar_unfold }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.source_layout { layout_module_storage_path }

// THE CLOSURE BOUNDARY: repository_ci_profile reads three of these rows and nothing else of the
// run-step roster, and the roster (gunbc.instruments.ci_run_step_roster) imports every step module whose
// target it enumerates. Declared here, the type and those rows cost a reader
// two modules instead of that world (every private witness resolved it through repository_ci_profile).

// This module holds the type and the three rows repository_ci_profile reads. The roster that joins every
// `gunbc run` step target is `gunbc_run_step_targets` in gunbc.instruments.ci_run_step_roster, and it
// stays the single roster.
//
// The pair was previously two string literals at each row, and that cost a real defect: a
// merge conflict resolution in gunbc#8377 re-authored two of them by hand, guessing paths from
// module names, and produced `dag/gunbc/spark/grant_install.dag` (never existed at any commit) and
// `dag/gunbc/spark/serving_durability.dag` (exists but does not define the named function, nor
// import the module that does). Nothing refused, because a path in a string is not a symbol — the
// gunbc.design_argument::single_authority stale-citation class, landing in an emitted argv rather than prose. Both steps
// were unrunnable on main from the day they landed. One roster gives one population to join
// against, instead of pairs scattered across call sites where two strings could disagree unnoticed.
//
// WHY BOTH EARLIER ENFORCEMENT ATTEMPTS WERE WITHDRAWN, so nobody rebuilds them: "does file F declare
// symbol G" is answered by decl_facts, which walks POOL ROOTS — directories, recursively, ~3833 modules,
// ~8s. By controlled A/B, an emit-time wall cost 180s across 22 call sites and took SEVEN pre-existing
// witness claims below verdict, because two witness modules render workflow steps and inherited the
// walk. The fast-lane ceiling is 5000ms, so the binding constraint is that NO CORPUS WALK MAY BE
// REACHABLE FROM A FAST-LANE CLAIM AT ALL — one walk breaches it. Nothing here walks: the derivation
// below is a pure function over gunbc.source_layout's literal storage-root rows.
//
// THE RUNG NOW REACHED (gunbc.plans.closure_consolidation P2a). A row carries a std.decl_ref
// DeclarationRef -- the module NAME and the function name -- and no longer authors a file path at all.
// The path half is DERIVED at render time by gunbc_run_step_target_entry_path, which delegates to
// gunbc.source_layout layout_module_storage_path, the single name-to-path authority; consumers never
// hand-write it (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority). One authored fact now stands where two could
// disagree, and the disagreement the gunbc#8377 pair had was mechanically impossible to write any more:
// there is no path string to get wrong. The derived path still crosses the word wall at
// v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit gunbc_run_invocation_words, so a module name that derives a path
// containing shell metacharacters still refuses.
//
// THE ABSENT ARM REFUSES, IT DOES NOT FABRICATE (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed). A module name outside
// every registered storage root, or a bare or top-level name, derives no path; the target entry points
// in v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit then return a TYPED, located refusal THERE -- an Outcome rejection
// whose diagnostics carry the refused module_path and decl_name sanitized through that emitter's own
// character map (gunbc_invoke_sanitize_word, the family's only one) -- rather than any invented path and
// rather than a marker string. That typed refusal rides the invoke family out to the job body and is
// unwrapped ONCE at the generated-artifact boundary (gunbc.generated_artifact_emit artifact_generate) into
// a typed ArtifactGenerationRefused naming the refused row. The old __GUNBC_INVOKE_EMIT_REFUSED__ poison and
// the byte scan that hunted it in the committed output (gunbc.tier_o_artifact_emit) are DELETED together
// (replacement_migration, no fallback): the refusal never reaches the rendered bytes to be scanned for, so
// the gate no longer needs to read them. That is the wall this comment always said was owed at the gate,
// now standing on the types for the refusal itself rather than on a scan: a module that derives no path
// cannot be committed as a passing step, because its refusal is a value the producer must unwrap, not text
// it can accidentally pass through. The wall runs on EVERY
// path to committed workflow bytes because every producer passes
// through the gate's admitted point, and every roster row is rendered into at least one committed
// workflow. So: a row naming a module NO registered storage root contains cannot reach a committed
// workflow. That is enforced by code that executes.
//
// BOTH HALVES ARE NOW CHECKED, stated plainly because the comment must not overclaim. The module half is
// checked at emit (it derives a path or returns a typed refusal). The DECLARATION half -- `decl_name` -- was
// the residue: a row naming a real module and a nonexistent function derived a path, rendered, and failed only at
// workflow RUN time, when `gunbc run <derived-path> <function>` could not resolve the entry. That gap is now
// closed at the required job: v2.cli.reference_check check_references treats a call to THIS constructor as a
// resolution site and resolves its (module_path, decl_name) pair through the SAME target universe and native
// resolver it already builds for @ref markers, so a misspelled entry refuses there -- located at the constructing
// row -- instead of surviving to CI run time. The site is keyed on the callee's RESOLVED identity (it must
// resolve, through the caller's imports in the check's own ResolutionContext, to this constructor's declaring
// home), never on the call's spelling, and a non-literal argument refuses typed rather than being skipped
// (fail_closed). The gunbc#8377 class "exists but does not define the named function" is therefore refused in the
// required fast-lane step.
//
// THE RUNG THIS IS, AND THE RUNG THAT IS NOT (the rung ladder, @ref(gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder)).
// This is rung 2, mechanically preventable: the gate reliably exposes and blocks the typo, but the entry is still
// an authored string, so the safety depends on the check RUNNING and staying enrolled -- it is the check
// executing, not a guarantee in the types. The TERMINAL form is rung 3: a TYPED declaration reference, in which
// the entry is not a string at all but a reference that names a declaration through its import, so a bad entry is
// a compile error and no check need run. That is the compiler's resolved symbol identity (v2.compiler name_resolve
// ResolutionContext / SymbolIndex, or the demand engine once it supplies a declaration index); until that lands,
// this required-job resolution is the rung that actually catches the typo. NOTE the fast-lane constraint that
// shaped this and still holds: check_references resolves only the DEMANDED modules (the cited targets, each
// caller, and this constructor's home) -- never a corpus walk from a fast-lane claim. A SIBLING RUNG on this wall
// has LANDED: the invoke-family entry refusal (this path plus the emitter's word-wall) is now a typed Outcome
// unwrapped once at the artifact boundary, and the Tier O prefix SCAN with its __GUNBC_INVOKE_EMIT_REFUSED__ poison
// are deleted together -- that threading is integration concern `emitter_string_return_carries_no_typed_refusal`
// (gunbc.integration_concern), now Integrated. The ORCHESTRATION poison (__GUNBC_ORCH_EMIT_REFUSED__) is a separate
// token produced by a different module and is recorded as its own concern row for the same Outcome cutover.
type GunbcRunStepTarget {
  declaration: DeclarationRef
}

// THE ONE DERIVATION FROM TARGET TO ENTRY PATH, beside the type it reads (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority):
// the module name through gunbc.source_layout layout_module_storage_path, a pure function over the
// layout rows with no filesystem read. Present carries the derived workflow-visible path; Absent means
// the module belongs to no registered storage root, and every consumer must refuse, never fabricate.
fn gunbc_run_step_target_entry_path(target: GunbcRunStepTarget) -> Optional<String> {
  layout_module_storage_path(module: target.declaration.module_path as String)
}

// THE ENTRY AS WRITTEN BY A ROW: module name plus function name, via the std.decl_ref constructor with
// field WholeDeclaration. Rows do not hand-build the record, so no row can carry a field coordinate or
// skip the constructor that keeps the identity whole.
fn gunbc_run_step_target(module: String, function: String) -> GunbcRunStepTarget {
  GunbcRunStepTarget { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: module, decl_name: function) }
}

data gunbc_ci_tier_o_drift_check_target: GunbcRunStepTarget = gunbc_run_step_target(
  module: "gunbc.instruments.tier_o_drift_check",
  function: "main",
)

data gunbc_ci_heal_publication_admit_target: GunbcRunStepTarget = gunbc_run_step_target(
  module: "gunbc.heal_publication",
  function: "heal_publication_admit_wet",
)

data gunbc_ci_heal_publication_publish_target: GunbcRunStepTarget = gunbc_run_step_target(
  module: "gunbc.heal_publication",
  function: "heal_publication_publish_wet",
)
